---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const tools = [
  { name: 'Simulator', href: '/simulator/', text: 'Renders phones, book and flip foldables, dual-screen devices, multi-folds, tablets and desktop windows on iOS and Android, with postures, window states, overlays, collision checks and a side-by-side platform comparison.' },
  { name: 'Figma plugin', href: 'https://github.com/jacksonmafra-umain/Dobra/tree/main/packages/figma-plugin', text: 'Creates tagged artboards with hinge overlays and grids, shows which device postures a file covers, checks frames against the foldable rules and adapts a frame to another target.' },
  { name: 'Web report', href: '/report/', text: "Opens a Figma file or a report JSON and shows the file's coverage and the rule findings per frame, with thumbnails and downloads." },
  { name: 'CLI', href: 'https://github.com/jacksonmafra-umain/Dobra/tree/main/packages/cli', text: 'Checks a website in Chromium at every device target with fold emulation, and writes the same report the other tools read.' },
];
const installer = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jacksonmafra-umain/Dobra/main/install.sh';
---
<Base title="Dobra" description="Tools for designing foldable and dual-screen UIs on iOS and Android: a simulator, a Figma plugin, a web report and a website checker." path="/">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Design for every fold.</h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">Dobra covers phones, book and flip foldables, dual-screen devices, multi-folds, tablets and desktop, on iOS and Android.</p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="button button--primary" href="/simulator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the simulator</a>
      <a class="button" href="/guide/">Read the guide</a>
    </div>
    <video class="hero__video" controls muted playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/dobra-launch-poster.jpg">
      <source src="/media/dobra-launch-720.mp4" type="video/mp4" media="(max-width: 800px)" />
      <source src="/media/dobra-launch.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
    </video>
  </section>
  <section class="tools" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <h2 id="tools-title">The tools</h2>
    <div class="tools__grid">
      {
        tools.map((t) => (
          <a class="tool" href={t.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <h3>{t.name}</h3>
            <p>{t.text}</p>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="quickstart" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <h2 id="install-title">Install on your Mac</h2>
    <p>No GitHub, Node or admin rights needed. Open Terminal and paste this line:</p>
    <pre><code>bash -c "$(curl -fsSL {installer})"</code></pre>
    <p>
      Or download the <a href="https://github.com/jacksonmafra-umain/Dobra/archive/refs/heads/main.zip" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ZIP</a>, unzip it
      and run <code>bash install.sh</code> in that folder. It takes a few minutes the first time. Then, in a new Terminal
      window:
    </p>
    <pre><code>dobra simulator          # open the simulator
dobra report             # open the web report and check websites
dobra plugin             # add the Figma plugin to Figma desktop
dobra check site https://example.com
dobra update             # get the latest version</code></pre>
    <h3 id="plugin-title">Add the Figma plugin</h3>
    <p>The plugin runs in the Figma desktop app, not in the browser. Add it once:</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Run <code>dobra plugin</code>. It opens Figma and shows the plugin's <code>manifest.json</code> in Finder.</li>
      <li>In Figma, open any design file, then go to <strong>Plugins › Development › Import plugin from manifest…</strong></li>
      <li>Choose <code>~/Dobra/packages/figma-plugin/manifest.json</code>, the file Finder shows.</li>
      <li>Run it from <strong>Plugins › Development › Dobra</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>After <code>dobra update</code>, Figma loads the new version the next time you run the plugin. The <a href="https://github.com/jacksonmafra-umain/Dobra/blob/main/docs/figma-plugin/guide.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">plugin guide</a> walks through each tab.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="quickstart" aria-labelledby="qs-title">
    <h2 id="qs-title">For developers</h2>
    <pre><code>npm install
npm run dev            # simulator
npm run dev:report     # web report
npm run build:cli && npm run dobra -- check site https://example.com</code></pre>
  </section>
</Base>
